CM ============================================================
CM NEC-2 Model: 40m Half-Wave Dipole
CM Document:    TM-HFTN-NEC-002
CM Author:      Merv Martin
CM Date:        2026-05-02
CM ============================================================
CM Description:
CM   Horizontal half-wave dipole for the 40m amateur band.
CM   Center frequency: 7.15 MHz
CM   Total length: 20.98m (lambda/2 = 300/7.15/2 = 20.979m)
CM   Height above ground: 12m (~0.286 lambda)
CM   Wire: AWG 12 copper, radius = 0.001m
CM
CM Ground model: Real (Sommerfeld-Norton, Type 1)
CM   Conductivity (sigma): 0.005 S/m  (average ground)
CM   Relative permittivity (epsilon_r): 13
CM
CM Coordinate system:
CM   X-axis: along wire
CM   Half-wire: x = -10.49m to +10.49m at z = 12m
CM   Y-axis: broadside to dipole
CM
CM Frequency sweep: 7.000 to 7.300 MHz, 7 steps (~50 kHz spacing)
CM Source: voltage source at junction of left and right halves
CM
CM Expected results:
CM   Resonance near 7.15 MHz: ~70 + j0 ohms
CM   Gain: ~8.0 dBi broadside (ground reflection gain)
CM   Elevation angle of max radiation: ~30 deg at 12m height
CM   NVIS component significant at 12m (< lambda/4 = 10.49m)
CM --- GEOMETRY ---
CM Left half: x = -10.49m to x = 0
CM Right half: x = 0 to x = +10.49m
CM Ground
CM --- GROUND PARAMETERS ---
CM --- EXCITATION ---
CM Source at last segment of left half (wire 1, segment 20) = feed point
CM --- FREQUENCY SWEEP ---
CM 7 frequencies: 7.000, 7.050, 7.100, 7.150, 7.200, 7.250, 7.300 MHz
CM --- CURRENT DISTRIBUTION PRINT ---
CM --- RADIATION PATTERNS ---
CM Elevation pattern (E-plane, phi=0, theta 0-90 deg, step 2 deg)
CM Azimuth pattern (H-plane, theta=60 deg = 30 deg elevation, step 5 deg)
CM NVIS pattern (near-vertical, theta=0-30 deg, fine resolution 1 deg)
CM ============================================================
CM NOTES:
CM   Segment count: 20 per half = 40 total segments.
CM   Segment length at 7.15 MHz: 10.49/20 = 0.524m.
CM   Minimum segments/wavelength at 7.3 MHz: 40.98m / 0.524m = ~78.
CM   NEC-2 guideline: >10 seg/wavelength satisfied.
CM
CM   The wire tag numbering convention:
CM     Wire 1: left half (negative x to 0)
CM     Wire 2: right half (0 to positive x)
CM   Source placed at end of wire 1 = electrical centre.
CM
CM TYPICAL OUTPUT (7.15 MHz):
CM   Impedance:    ~73 + j0 ohms at resonance
CM   Max gain:     ~8.2 dBi (over real Sommerfeld-Norton ground)
CM   Max elev:     ~28-32 degrees above horizon at 12m
CM   Broadside dir: y-axis (±90 deg azimuth)
CM   End-fire:     ~3-4 dB down from broadside
CM
CM BAND COVERAGE:
CM   7.000-7.300 MHz (40m CW/phone) — SWR < 2:1 over 100 kHz
CM   bandwidth centered at resonant frequency.
CM ============================================================
CE
GW  1   20  -10.49  0.0   12.0   0.0    0.0   12.0   0.001
GW  2   20   0.0    0.0   12.0   10.49  0.0   12.0   0.001
GE  1
GN  2   0   0   0   13.0   0.005
EX  0   1   20   00   1.0   0.0
FR  0   7   0   0   7.000   0.050
PQ  0   0   0   0
RP  0   46   1   1001   0.0   0.0   2.0   0.0
RP  0   1   73   1001   60.0   0.0   0.0   5.0
RP  0   31   1   1001   0.0   0.0   1.0   0.0
